8. Self‑Fueling Regime Integration

Plunk et al. (2026) introduced SQuID‑\tau, a self‑fueling quasi‑isodynamic stellarator sustaining density peaking via inward turbulent particle transport, with C_p = -\Gamma_{\text{turb}} / \nabla n > 0 [16]. The NTCS controller monitors the particle pinch coefficient through the surrogate head H_\phi^\Gamma and adjusts ECRH deposition to maintain C_p > C_p^{\text{threshold}} while avoiding impurity accumulation.

