9. Conclusion

We have presented the Neural Turbulence‑Controlled Stellarator (NTCS) framework with appropriate mathematical rigor. Starting from the Hamiltonian formulation of gyrokinetic dynamics and the experimentally validated predator‑prey model of turbulence‑zonal‑flow interactions, we built a latent neural surrogate grounded in Fourier Neural Operators with physical consistency constraints and conformal safety filters. The control problem is formulated as stochastic optimal control with explicit assumptions on Lipschitz continuity, actuator bounds, and timescale separation.

The key conceptual shift remains:

\text{Static stellarator design} \quad \longrightarrow \quad \text{Adaptive, learning‑based plasma control.}

The framework provides a realistic, technically specified pathway toward real‑time turbulence control on W7‑X and next‑generation stellarators, while being explicit about its scope and limitations.


